  "chrome": {
    "$comment": "The chrome roles: the page background, the card fill, body ink, the muted fill and its ink, the hairline, the input boundary, the focus ring, and the primary action colour with its ink. Every component renders these. Before this block they lived only as raw oklch values in app/product.css, at grey hues that did not sit on the neutral ladder, so the contrast gate measured a page that was not the page that rendered. Holding them here gives scripts/build-tokens.mts a source of truth and makes the audited page the rendered page. Each role names a ladder step where one exists and states an explicit oklch only where none does. Declared per theme. The honest residual, which this makes visible and does not fix: ring at chroma 0.13 and primary at chroma 0.135 are as chromatic as the category axis, whose labs seed is 0.11, so calling these roles neutral is wrong. That is a design question for a human, not a value to tune here. Values are fixed by DECISIONS.md D5. mutedForeground follows product-theme-and-tokens-02.a; border and input follow product-theme-and-tokens-07.a.",
