  "categoryExtensionExample": {
    "$comment": "NOT SHIPPED. The worked example used by /docs/theming/category-palettes. A product that tracks menstrual cycles needs a seventh category; adding one is a seed plus a run of the ladder, and it must not borrow a hue that is already carrying a status. Hue 340 sits clear of urgent (27), attention (45), watch (82) and steady (178), and clear of heart (15).",
    "cycle": {
      "label": "Cycle",
      "seed": {
        "l": 0.64,
        "c": 0.13,
        "h": 340,
        "srgb": "oklch(0.64 0.13 340)"
      }
    }
  },
  "colourIndependence": {
    "$comment": "A MEASURED FINDING, not a claim. lib/color/cvd.ts was run over the four status accents and the six category accents under protanopia, deuteranopia, tritanopia and grayscale, and the pairs below fall below the Lc 15 collapse threshold. As flat fills they become hard or impossible to tell apart. scripts/check-contrast.mts regenerates this audit into lib/generated/contrast.json and <CvdSimulator> renders it. The numbers here are a snapshot for authors, rounded to one decimal place, and they are the exception named under `floor`: the published ones are the generated ones, and nothing gates this copy against them. The snapshot lists only pairs among the four status levels. `unknown` collides with several of them and is deliberately absent, because it is the absence of an assertion rather than a fifth level, and a table that ranked it beside the four would teach the wrong model; the generated audit carries those pairs in full.",
    "method": "Viénot, Brettel and Mollon (1999) dichromacy projection in linear-light sRGB, plus a relative-luminance grayscale. Full severity. An approximation of dichromacy, not a model of any individual reader.",
    "collapseThresholdLc": 15,
    "finding": "The status axis collapses in pairs, and it collapses across nearly every simulation now that the four accents are packed into the narrow lightness band the non-text floor leaves on a near-white page. Measured over the current accents with lib/color/cvd.ts: under tritanopia all six pairs fall to Lc 0; under deuteranopia five of the six do; under grayscale both steady and watch, and watch and attention, fall to Lc 0, so a reader ranking bands by weight on a dial or a bar cannot separate those fills. This is not a defect a different hue would fix. Four ordered levels sharing roughly 0.10 of lightness cannot be made mutually distinguishable by fill alone for every form of colour vision, and that lightness band is fixed from above by the rule that each accent must also clear the non-text contrast floor against the page and against its own surface. The lighter spread the report proposed was measured and rejected here because it drops steady and watch back below that floor, which is the failure the re-seed existed to remove. The system answers the collapse the only way it can, by never letting colour carry status alone.",
    "consequence": "It is the reason colour is never the sole carrier of status in this system. Every status level ships colour PLUS an icon PLUS a word, and the icons are chosen to differ in silhouette rather than only in colour. A product that renders a bare coloured dot to mean status has broken the system, and OPSIN-0002 fires on it in development.",
    "statusCollisions": [
      {
        "type": "protanopia",
        "pair": ["steady", "watch"],
        "lc": 10.9
      },
      {
        "type": "protanopia",
        "pair": ["watch", "attention"],
        "lc": 7.7
      },
      {
        "type": "protanopia",
        "pair": ["attention", "urgent"],
        "lc": 11
      },
      {
        "type": "deuteranopia",
        "pair": ["steady", "watch"],
        "lc": 0
      },
      {
        "type": "deuteranopia",
        "pair": ["steady", "attention"],
        "lc": 0
      },
